<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      IntraFlow ships outside the App Store and is not sandboxed, so it does NOT
      need the app-sandbox entitlement.

      Notarization requires only the Hardened Runtime flag, which the release
      workflow adds through the codesign "options runtime" argument. Sandboxing
      is a separate, stricter mode and is not required for direct distribution.

      This dictionary is deliberately empty: add an entitlement here only when a
      capability genuinely requires one. The usual candidates, should a future
      feature need them, are the network client entitlement and the JIT
      entitlement. Neither is needed today, because the app reaches the network
      only through sockets it already owns and WebKit needs no JIT entitlement
      outside the sandbox.

      Keep this file free of double hyphens inside comments: the code signing
      tooling rejects them, unlike plutil.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
